.TH STYLER 1 "August 2026" "Styler" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
styler \- build, apply and remove reproducible Linux changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B styler
.br
.B styler change
.I ACTION
.br
.B styler constructor
.I ACTION
.br
.B styler baseline
.I ACTION
.br
.B styler package
.I ACTION
.SH DESCRIPTION
Styler provides a catalog of semantic Linux changes and a unified Change Constructor. The constructor selects a baseline, detects applications and visual resources, synthesizes an internal recipe, compiles a PipeCraft DAG, and exports the result.
.PP
The only portable file extension is
.BR .stylerpkg .
A package may contain either a baseline or a change, as declared by its manifest.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B styler change --help
Plan, integrate, or remove catalog changes.
.TP
.B styler constructor --help
Scan the system, build an automatic plan, and export a change package.
.TP
.B styler baseline --help
Capture, select, import, export, repair, or delete baselines.
.TP
.B styler package --help
Inspect, import, export, or delete .stylerpkg files. Change packages are applied from the change command, not directly from package management.

.SH CONSTRUCTOR EXIT STATUS
.B styler constructor export
returns 0 when every selected element was included. It returns 1 when a package was created with omissions; each omission is printed as an
.B OMITIDO
line with its reason.

.SH BUILT-IN YAML CHANGES
Styler can load built-in declarative YAML changes and compile them to the same PipeCraft workflow used by the Changes interface. AppImageLauncher and Affinity for Linux are the first two built-in YAML changes. Affinity depends on AppImageLauncher; selecting Affinity composes both definitions automatically. The bundled provider is limited to Ubuntu/Debian-family x86_64 systems. Before downloading AppImageLauncher, Styler checks the YAML-declared ail-cli capability and reuses an existing installation when available.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/styler
Default Styler library.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/styler/.styler
Internal state, runs, receipts, baselines, and indexes.
.SH SAFETY
Importing a package never executes it. Execution requires an explicit plan and approval.

.SH BASELINE CATALOG AUTHORING
The Tools constructor can export the selected baseline as-is, or prepare a separate official catalog candidate. The latter requires explicit confirmation that the capture came from a clean installation and leaves the local custom baseline unchanged. Place the resulting .stylerpkg in styler/baselines/catalog/ before building a later release.

.SH IDENTIFICADORES DE PAQUETE
Al crear paquetes, Styler normaliza automáticamente el texto humano a un identificador seguro. La validación de paquetes importados permanece estricta.
